## Real-data bug fixes (§2b.15)
1. geom.py: back-to-back duplicate triangles (same 3 vertices, opposite winding) in 290 raw triangles (joint 217, muscle 44,
   nerve 11, organ 10, bone 4, tendon 4) cancelled the area-weighted normal to zero; zero-area triangles (e.g. half of
   Spinal dura, 10,100 tris) gave zero normals too. Attempt 1 packs had 5,634 skin + ~4,800 anatomy vertices with |n| < 0.9.
   Fix: new geom.clean(part) drops duplicate and zero-area (|cross| <= 1e-12) triangles and unused vertices; geom.run
   calls it before outward() and again after decimate_parts() (fast_simplification also leaves cancelling faces).
2. geom.py: vertex_normals falls back to the radial direction from the part centre where the normal still cancels
   (|sum| <= 1e-6 x sum of face areas) or the vertex has no faces (MakeHuman skin has 5,634 vertices outside the
   body/eye groups; they stay so skin vertex ids keep MakeHuman's numbering). All packed normals now have length 0.9-1.1.
3. sex.py: MALE_ONLY and EXTERNAL matched "testi" inside "Juxta-intestinal mesenteric nodes" (flagged male-only and
   external). Fix: \btesti. Male-only parts 26 -> 25, ext 18 -> 17.

